WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:10.090
Together we've increased early childhood education.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.570
Lifted high school graduation rates to new
highs.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.340
Boosted graduates in fields like engineering.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:21.690
In his last State of the Union address, President
Obama mentioned that graduation rates in our

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.860
nation's public high schools are at an all-time
high.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.189
He's absolutely correct.

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:30.600
Eighty-two percent of our public high school
students graduate from our schools.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.160
Here's the challenge.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:37.260
There's also a rise in the number of students
who enrolled in post-secondary education institutions

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.969
with need for remediation in English Language
Arts and Mathematics.

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:42.969
That's troubling.

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:46.780
For one reason, President Obama say we should
increase the number of engineers that we have

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.920
in our schools.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.949
Well guess what?

00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:52.719
In order to have more engineers, we'd need
to make sure that we have teachers in place

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.089
at the high school level, working in his or
her field to train more engineers.

00:00:57.089 --> 00:01:01.539
But secondly, we cannot rely on the public
school sector alone to increase the number

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:05.030
of engineers or the number of entrepreneurs
that we need in our nation.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.290
That's going to take private sector choice,
something that I wish the President would

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.380
have supported more in his administration.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.610
But with the next administration coming forward,
school choice along with public schools will

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.720
make this nation great.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.560
So what are you thoughts about President Obama's
legacy on education?

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:26.190
And check out other AEI scholars' response
to President Obama's State of the Union.

